{"term":"stout","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:e1777d0509e70f293b","definition":"Large; bulky.","example":"Yossarian walked out of the office and down the stairs into the dark, tomblike street, passing in the hall the stout woman with warts and two chins, who was already on her way back in.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["thickset","corpulent","fat"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["midstout","overstout","stouten","stouthearted","stoutish","stout-legged moa","stoutly","stoutness","unstout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3514c3b6128942207e","definition":"Bold, strong-minded.","example":"Art thou but Captaine of a thouſand horſe,\nThat by Characters grauen in thy browes,\nAnd by thy martiall face and ſtout aſpect,\nDeſeru’ſt to haue the leading of an hoſte?","pos":"adj","synonyms":["lusty","vigorous","robust","sinewy","muscular"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["midstout","overstout","stouten","stouthearted","stoutish","stout-legged moa","stoutly","stoutness","unstout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f69b4f61b8eda96059","definition":"Proud; haughty.","example":"Your words have been stout against me.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["arrogant","hard","haughty"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["midstout","overstout","stouten","stouthearted","stoutish","stout-legged moa","stoutly","stoutness","unstout"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stout#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:11310c6e047cb2b4f6","definition":"Fir